---
layout: default
---
{%- comment -%}
  Home-page order is deliberate and reads top-to-bottom as an argument:

    identity  → who this is
    thesis    → what they work on, scannable
    proof     → why you should keep reading
    substance → what the work actually asks - research threads
    evidence  → the receipts - selected publications
    new(s)    → that it is still happening
    onward    → where to go next
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="home-hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Ph.D. Student · Arizona State University</p>
  <h1>{{ site.title }}</h1>
  <p class="home-hero__lead">{{ page.hero | default: site.subtitle }}</p>

  <ul class="research-areas" aria-label="Research areas">
    {%- for area in site.research_areas -%}<li>{{ area }}</li>{%- endfor -%}
  </ul>

  <div class="bio">{{ content }}</div>
  {% include social.liquid %}
</section>

<ul class="highlights" aria-label="Highlights">
  {%- for h in site.data.highlights -%}
  <li class="highlights__item">
    <span class="highlights__label">{{ h.label }}</span>
    <span class="highlights__detail">{{ h.detail }}</span>
  </li>
  {%- endfor -%}
</ul>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section__head">
    <h2>What I Work On</h2>
    <a href="{{ '/publications/' | relative_url }}">the papers →</a>
  </div>
  <div class="threads">
    {%- for t in site.data.research -%}
    <article class="thread">
      <span class="thread__icon" aria-hidden="true">{% include icon.liquid name=t.icon %}</span>
      <div class="thread__body">
        <h3 class="thread__name">{{ t.name }}</h3>
        <p class="thread__q">{{ t.question }}</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="thread__evidence">
        {%- for e in t.evidence -%}<li>{{ e }}</li>{%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </article>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section__head">
    <h2>Selected Publications</h2>
    <a href="{{ '/publications/' | relative_url }}">all publications →</a>
  </div>
  {% include pub-list.liquid selected=true %}
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section__head">
    <h2>Recent news</h2>
    <a href="{{ '/news/' | relative_url }}">all news →</a>
  </div>
  {%- comment -%}
    Three, not six. The home page is a selection; /news/ is the archive. Six
    entries reached back to 2023 and turned the section into a changelog.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% include news-list.liquid limit=3 %}
</section>

<div class="section__head">
  <h2>Explore</h2>
</div>
<nav class="quicklinks" aria-label="Explore the site">
  <a class="quicklink" href="{{ '/publications/' | relative_url }}">
    {% include icon.liquid name="doc" %}
    <span class="quicklink__title">Publications</span>
    <span class="quicklink__desc">Papers out of the mill</span>
  </a>
  <a class="quicklink" href="{{ '/projects/' | relative_url }}">
    {% include icon.liquid name="grid" %}
    <span class="quicklink__title">Projects</span>
    <span class="quicklink__desc">Things I've built &amp; broken</span>
  </a>
  <a class="quicklink" href="{{ '/cv/' | relative_url }}">
    {% include icon.liquid name="file" %}
    <span class="quicklink__title">CV</span>
    <span class="quicklink__desc">The long-form story</span>
  </a>
</nav>
</section>
